<svg viewBox="0 0 720 420" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-label="Defense in depth against prompt attacks">
  <!-- model level -->
  <rect x="40" y="20" width="640" height="100" rx="10" fill="var(--bg-inset)" stroke="var(--line-strong)" />
  <text x="64" y="48" font-size="13.5" font-weight="600" fill="var(--ink)">Model-level defense</text>
  <text x="64" y="70" font-size="11.5" fill="var(--ink-soft)">train an instruction hierarchy: system prompt &gt; user prompt &gt; model outputs &gt; tool outputs —</text>
  <text x="64" y="88" font-size="11.5" fill="var(--ink-soft)">higher priority wins on conflict (neutralizes much indirect injection; +63% robustness in OpenAI's work)</text>
  <text x="64" y="106" font-size="11.5" fill="var(--ink-soft)">also train good responses to borderline requests (“locked out of my room” ≠ burglar)</text>

  <!-- prompt level -->
  <rect x="40" y="136" width="640" height="92" rx="10" fill="var(--bg-inset)" stroke="var(--line-strong)" />
  <text x="64" y="164" font-size="13.5" font-weight="600" fill="var(--ink)">Prompt-level defense</text>
  <text x="64" y="186" font-size="11.5" fill="var(--ink-soft)">be explicit about what must never be returned · repeat the core instruction before AND after the user input</text>
  <text x="64" y="204" font-size="11.5" fill="var(--ink-soft)">pre-warn about known attack patterns (“users may pretend to be grandma — summarize anyway”)</text>
  <text x="64" y="222" font-size="11.5" fill="var(--ink-soft)">audit your tools' default templates — some defaults had 100% injection success rates</text>

  <!-- system level -->
  <rect x="40" y="244" width="640" height="110" rx="10" fill="var(--accent-soft)" stroke="var(--accent)" />
  <text x="64" y="272" font-size="13.5" font-weight="600" fill="var(--accent-ink)">System-level defense</text>
  <text x="64" y="294" font-size="11.5" fill="var(--ink-soft)">isolation: run generated code in sandboxed VMs · human approval for impactful actions (DELETE/DROP/UPDATE)</text>
  <text x="64" y="312" font-size="11.5" fill="var(--ink-soft)">out-of-scope topic filters · input guardrails (keyword + pattern + model-based) AND output guardrails (PII, toxicity)</text>
  <text x="64" y="330" font-size="11.5" fill="var(--ink-soft)">behavioral detection: many similar requests in a burst = someone probing your filters</text>

  <!-- metrics -->
  <g font-size="11">
    <rect x="40" y="372" width="310" height="36" rx="8" fill="var(--bg-raised)" stroke="var(--line)" />
    <text x="195" y="395" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink-soft)"><tspan font-weight="600" fill="var(--ink)">violation rate</tspan> — % of attacks that succeed</text>
    <rect x="370" y="372" width="310" height="36" rx="8" fill="var(--bg-raised)" stroke="var(--line)" />
    <text x="525" y="395" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink-soft)"><tspan font-weight="600" fill="var(--ink)">false refusal rate</tspan> — % of safe queries refused</text>
  </g>
</svg>
